-- הסכם עוז לתמורה (14.8.2011), §39 תוספת שחיקה: from 1.9.2011 the teaching
-- employees are given a supplement of 2.1% on the combined salary and the
-- 1987, 1994, 2008 and 2001 supplements, for the erosion of their pay
-- against the engineers' in 2008–2010 ("תוספת שחיקה 2011"); a separate
-- component, in the base of the percentage supplements on the combined
-- salary save four, and of the hour value, severance and the pension,
-- training and Dafna funds.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT vocabulary
IMPORT conventions
IMPORT `oz-founding-common`
IMPORT `oz-founding-16`
IMPORT `oz-founding-38`
IMPORT `oz-founding-20`
IMPORT `1995-09-12_oz-latmura_special-agreement-hashlama`

§ `39 תוספת שחיקה`

§§ `39(א)`

-- (א): from 1.9.2011 (the day included: convention dates.start) the
-- teaching employees (part י speaks of all of them) are entitled to a
-- supplement of 2.1%, computed on the combined salary, the 1987, 1994, 2008
-- and 2001 supplements, for the erosion of teaching employees' pay against
-- the engineers' in 2008–2010, under the collective agreements between the
-- parties of 11.5.1993 and 12.9.1995. The rate and the base are this
-- section's own; the two agreements are the mechanism it was measured by.
-- The agreement of 12.9.95 (imported) sets no formula of its own: its §ב.1
-- puts a change of the 1993 agreement's erosion check to a joint committee
-- on four proposals, and its §ב.2 pays the 1996 table by the check.
@ref akn:art_39__para_a
`the erosion supplement rate` MEANS 2.1%

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the combined salary` IS A NUMBER @desc the teaching employee's own, at his position
      `the 1987 supplement` IS A NUMBER
      `the 1994 supplement` IS A NUMBER
      `the 2008 supplement` IS A NUMBER
      `the 2001 supplement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the erosion supplement under section 39` d `the combined salary` `the 1987 supplement` `the 1994 supplement` `the 2008 supplement` `the 2001 supplement` IS
    IF d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2011)
    THEN `the erosion supplement rate` TIMES
             (`the combined salary` PLUS `the 1987 supplement` PLUS `the 1994 supplement` PLUS `the 2008 supplement` PLUS `the 2001 supplement`)
    ELSE 0

`why the erosion agreement of 11.5.1993 is not imported` MEANS
    `outside the corpus` "ההסכם הקיבוצי בין ארגון המורים לבין המעסיקים מיום 11.5.1993 (נוסחת בדיקת השחיקה ומנגנון השחיקה)"

`the proposals on the erosion check §39 measures by` MEANS `the proposals the 1995 Oz agreement puts to the erosion committee`

§§ `39(ב)`

-- (ב): the erosion supplement is paid as a separate salary component and is
-- brought into account for the percentage supplements computed on the
-- combined salary — save the 2001 supplement, the 2008 supplement, the Oz
-- LaTmura supplement and the 2011 supplement — and for the hour value,
-- severance pay under the Severance Pay Law, and contributions to a pension
-- provident fund, a training fund and the Dafna fund. (Its own base is
-- (א)'s: it is not in it.)
@ref akn:art_39__para_b
`the erosion supplement is a separate salary component` MEANS TRUE

GIVEN p IS A `what an Oz salary component counts for`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 39(ב)'s words bring the erosion supplement into` p IF
        NOT p EQUALS `computing supplement 2001`
    AND NOT p EQUALS `computing supplement 2008`
    AND NOT p EQUALS `computing the Oz LaTmura supplement`
    AND NOT p EQUALS `computing supplement 2011`
    AND NOT p EQUALS `computing erosion supplement 2011`

-- F-oz-founding-39-a: the exceptions leave out the promotion-grade
-- supplement, which §§16(ב) and 38(ג) name, so by its words (ב) brings the
-- erosion supplement into the promotion grade's base; §20(ה) says, "למען
-- הסר ספק", that no supplement is in it, those brought into the
-- percentage supplements on the combined salary among them. The reading
-- adopted (convention precedence.specific): §20(ה), which speaks of that
-- base, governs; the erosion supplement is not in it.
GIVEN p IS A `what an Oz salary component counts for`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the erosion supplement under section 39 counts for` p IF
        `section 39(ב)'s words bring the erosion supplement into` p
    AND (   NOT p EQUALS `computing the promotion-grade supplement`
         OR `section 20(ה) lets another supplement into the promotion grade's base`)

§§ `39 -- illustrations`

-- A combined salary of 10,000, 1987 and 1994 supplements of 400 and 500,
-- 2008 and 2001 supplements of 200 and 300: 2.1% of 11,400.
#ASSERT `the erosion supplement under section 39` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2011) 10000 400 500 200 300 EQUALS 239.4
#ASSERT `the erosion supplement under section 39` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2011) 10000 400 500 200 300 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the erosion supplement under section 39 counts for` `computing the hour value` AND `the erosion supplement under section 39 counts for` `contributions to the Dafna fund`
#ASSERT `the erosion supplement under section 39 counts for` `computing another percentage supplement on the combined salary`
#ASSERT NOT `the erosion supplement under section 39 counts for` `computing supplement 2011`
#ASSERT NOT `the erosion supplement under section 39 counts for` `computing the Oz LaTmura supplement`
-- the agreement of 12.9.95 sets no rate §39 could take: the 2.1% is §39's
#ASSERT NOT `the 1995 Oz agreement sets an erosion formula of its own`
#ASSERT count `the proposals on the erosion check §39 measures by` EQUALS 4

-- F-oz-founding-39-a's evidence: by (ב)'s words the erosion supplement
-- enters the promotion grade's base, and by §20(ה) it does not.
`section 39(ב) brings the erosion supplement into the promotion grade that section 20(ה) keeps it out of` MEANS
        `section 39(ב)'s words bring the erosion supplement into` `computing the promotion-grade supplement`
    AND NOT `the erosion supplement under section 39 counts for` `computing the promotion-grade supplement`
#ASSERT `section 39(ב) brings the erosion supplement into the promotion grade that section 20(ה) keeps it out of`

-- §§16(ב) and 39(ב) keep each other's supplement out of their bases, both
-- ways; so do §§38(ג) and 39(ב).
#ASSERT (NOT `the Oz LaTmura supplement counts for` `computing erosion supplement 2011`) AND (NOT `the erosion supplement under section 39 counts for` `computing the Oz LaTmura supplement`)
#ASSERT (NOT `the 2011 supplement under section 38 counts for` `computing erosion supplement 2011`) AND (NOT `the erosion supplement under section 39 counts for` `computing supplement 2011`)
